    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`POST /api/owners` now assigns each new owner a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `SMI-0007`), where LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and NNNN is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence one greater than the current owner count.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility OfficeFloor step that reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes the prefix from the last name, derives the sequence as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, and sets the code. It runs *before* `SaveOwner`, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct maps it by name in `toOwnerDto`), and it surfaces on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table.\n\n## Design notes\n\n- The sequence being count-based makes it global and monotonic across owners; because the step runs pre-save and Hibernate auto-flushes before the `findAll()` query, a just-created owner is included in the next owner's count \u2014 so consecutive creates increment by exactly 1, as the test asserts.\n- Logic lives in its own small step class rather than being bolted onto `BuildOwner` or `SaveOwner`, keeping each function single-purpose and reusing the existing `OwnerRepository`.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` (and the full suite) \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
